1
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,078
[HOST] Autumn 2003.

2
00:00:25,828 --> 00:00:29,543
At Somerset Medical Center in the
town of Somerville, New Jersey.

3
00:00:29,893 --> 00:00:34,097
Inside the intensive care unit bathed
in cold white fluorescent light,

4
00:00:34,097 --> 00:00:38,241
Charles Cullen was a familiar face
on the most grueling night shifts.

5
00:00:38,591 --> 00:00:42,687
The forty-three-year-old man had
a slight build, a gentle voice,

6
00:00:42,687 --> 00:00:44,863
always appeared with a mild smile,

7
00:00:44,863 --> 00:00:48,703
and was ever ready to cover
shifts for exhausted colleagues.

8
00:00:50,503 --> 00:00:53,767
[HOST] In a high-pressure clinical
environment where the boundary

9
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:56,525
between life and passing
was measured in seconds,

10
00:00:56,525 --> 00:00:59,733
Cullen was regarded as a
thoroughly dependable colleague.

11
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:04,725
He was always the first to rush over to
assist whenever a patient deteriorated,

12
00:01:04,725 --> 00:01:07,016
and the one who quietly tidied the room

13
00:01:07,016 --> 00:01:09,778
