resuscitation effort.

14
00:01:10,128 --> 00:01:12,844
To understand the depth of
that fondness and trust,

15
00:01:12,844 --> 00:01:16,145
let us listen to the reflections
of a nurse who stood shoulder

16
00:01:16,145 --> 00:01:19,021
to shoulder with him through
hundreds of night shifts.

17
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:24,881
[NURSE] In the eyes of every nurse among
us, Charlie was a wonderful friend.

18
00:01:25,231 --> 00:01:28,353
He was thoughtful, never lost his temper,

19
00:01:28,353 --> 00:01:33,532
and possessed extraordinarily gentle
hands when caring for patients.

20
00:01:33,882 --> 00:01:39,077
Whenever I was exhausted or unwell, he took
the initiative to shoulder the workload,

21
00:01:39,077 --> 00:01:43,159
even slipping me pain medication
to help me get through the shift.

22
00:01:43,509 --> 00:01:47,832
No one in the entire hospital
could have harbored the

23
00:01:47,832 --> 00:01:52,808
slightest suspicion about a man
so mild-mannered and devoted.

24
00:01:54,008 --> 00:01:56,547
[HOST] Yet behind those
scholarly wire-rimmed

25
00:01:56,547 --> 00:01:59,285
glasses and that pristine white lab coat,

26
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:03,494
a phantom of death was quietly
stalking the hospital corridors.

27
00:02:04,344 --> 00:02:08,775
On June 28th, 2003, sixty-eight-year-old
Father Florian Gall,

28
00:02:08,775 --> 00:02:11,317
former pastor in the Somerset area,

29
00:02:11,317 --> 00:02:15,385
was admitted for pneumonia
and infectious complications.

30
00:02:15,735 --> 00:02:19,903
His condition had stabilized and he
was preparing for discharge home.

31
00:02:21,253 --> 00:02:24,576
Yet mere hours after entering
Charles Cullen’s night shift,

32
00:02:24,576 --> 00:02:29,194
